# bg_basic.vexp - the hand-derived literal rows of the bg_basic video scenes (plan 04-11; D-156, D-157, D-158, D-161, D-169, D-171, D-172, D-173, ER-10, ER-11, ER-12, F-13).
# scripts/fixture-build writes this file, comments dropped, as build/gate/fixtures/bg-basic.vexp.tsv; the runner kind video (tests/conformance/videokinds.c) reads only that file. One source holds the literals: no expected value lives in a case file, and none comes from a run of DuoSpool, another emulator or a hash.
# The grammar is the one of vce_dot.vexp and vce_pal.vexp (scripts/lib/vexp-rules.awk); a ROWS selector may end in ;frame=F, the frame numbered F of the stream, because the guest sets its scene up over the first frames of the run.
# The fixture (fixtures/src/bg_basic.s) writes the vertical setup (VPR $0F02, VDW 239, VCR 4), HSR $0202 and HDR $031F (HDS 2, HDW 31: active_x 24, active_w 256 dots), MWR 0 (SCREEN 000: a 32 x 32 BAT, VM 0, SM 0), BXR = BYR = 0, the palette P(i) = (91 * i + 17) & 511, the BAT and seven tiles, then CR BB = 1 for six frames and MWR VM = 1 for four more frames.
# The frames: the numbers below were read from the guest's own sequence (the counted delays of bg_basic.s) on one run, as a calibration and never as a literal: frames 0 to 2 are the setup and burst frames, frames 3 to 8 draw the background, the MWR write falls in frame 8 before its VBlank entry,
# frames 9 to 11 are wholly after the latch and frame 12 is the partial last frame. A row at a frame that is not the intended one fails; it can never pass, because no other frame holds these indices.
# Display line K of a frame is the K-th record with an active window (line=active+K). With BYR = 0 the display line K shows virtual row K (D-156: bg_y = BYR at display line 0, then plus one): row K / 8 of the BAT, tile row K & 7. The dots of the window are virtual columns 0 to 255 (BXR = 0): BAT columns 0 to 31, tile column x & 7.
# The BAT (H7-14: word 0 is the top-left character, +1 to the right, +$20 per row; a word holds the bank in bits 15-12 and the code in bits 11-0): row 0 columns 0 to 3 are $3040, $0041, $F042 and $7043, every other word is $0040. The tiles (H7-15: 16 words from word code * 16; CG0 words 0 to 7 hold
# CH0 and CH1, CG1 words 8 to 15 hold CH2 and CH3; H7-18: VD3 to VD0 = CH3 to CH0, VD7 to VD4 = the bank, VD3 to VD0 all 0 forces VD7 to VD4 to 0):
#   code $040 solid pixel 15 (CH3 CH2 CH1 CH0 = 1111), code $041 solid pixel 12 (1100), code $042 solid pixel 3 (0011), code $043 pixel 0 everywhere.
# The indices (bank << 4) | pixel: column 0: bank 3, pixel 15: 48 + 15 = 63. Column 1: bank 0, pixel 12: 12. Column 2: bank 15, pixel 3: 240 + 3 = 243. Column 3: bank 7, pixel 0: the index is 0 whatever the bank (H7-18), not 112. Columns 4 to 31: bank 0, pixel 15: 15. So display line 0..7 reads 8 dots of 63, 8 of 12, 8 of 243, 8 of 0, then 224 of 15.
# The values (GUEST pal_bijection, ER-10: the weaker of MAN and GUEST): P(i) = (91 * i + 17) & 511 for every index i, written by the guest and read back against an additive sum (checks 5 and 6): P(63) = 5733 + 17 = 5750 = 11 * 512 + 118 = 118; P(12) = 1092 + 17 = 1109 = 2 * 512 + 85 = 85; P(243) =
# 22113 + 17 = 22130 = 43 * 512 + 114 = 114; P(0) = 17; P(15) = 1365 + 17 = 1382 = 2 * 512 + 358 = 358.
# The border (GUEST pal_bijection): palette entry $100 is P(256) = 23296 + 17 = 23313 = 45 * 512 + 273 = 273, and the header field border carries it on every record, judged a whole line after the last palette data write.
# Classes (ER-10): the structure rows use the 1365-clock grid and the frame length (ASSUMED LED-VID-0004). The index rows are MAN H7-18 (with the layout of H7-14 and H7-15): every tile is solid, so they hold for every bit order, byte order and flip; sym=order. The value rows rest on the guest's
# palette (GUEST pal_bijection). The solid group names no pixel order anywhere (ER-12).
# Kills (D-172): F1 shifts the dots of the focus line one dot to the right (a transition inside the x range turns the row red), F7 zeroes every non-zero index of that line; F2 (two index bits swapped) cannot act on the indices 63, 12, 243 and 0 (their two low bits are equal), so the solid groups do not declare it; F0 perturbs the first number of the first row.
scene	video_bg_basic_solid	case=video_bg_basic_solid	role=literal
group	video_bg_basic_solid	struct	form=STRUCT	class=ASSUMED:LED-VID-0004	sym=none	kills=F4,F8,F9
row	video_bg_basic_solid	struct	check=count	grid=1365
row	video_bg_basic_solid	struct	check=origins	step=1365
row	video_bg_basic_solid	struct	check=rec_bytes	header=64;version=1;max_w=682
row	video_bg_basic_solid	struct	check=values_below_512	limit=512
group	video_bg_basic_solid	solid	form=ROWS	class=MAN:H7-18	sym=order	kills=F0,F1,F7
row	video_bg_basic_solid	solid	line=active+0;x=0..31;frame=5	index=8*63,8*12,8*243,8*0
row	video_bg_basic_solid	solid	line=active+0;x=16..39;frame=5	index=8*243,8*0,8*15
row	video_bg_basic_solid	solid	line=active+7;x=0..31;frame=5	index=8*63,8*12,8*243,8*0
group	video_bg_basic_solid	solidval	form=ROWS	class=GUEST:pal_bijection	sym=order	kills=F0,F1
row	video_bg_basic_solid	solidval	line=active+0;x=0..31;frame=5	value=8*118,8*85,8*114,8*17
row	video_bg_basic_solid	solidval	line=active+0;x=16..39;frame=5	value=8*114,8*17,8*358
group	video_bg_basic_solid	border	form=STRUCT	class=GUEST:pal_bijection	sym=none	kills=F0
row	video_bg_basic_solid	border	check=border_after_pal	value=273
